# Last Message Project Rules

## Project Overview

Monorepo:

- `/backend` — Spring Boot 4 + WebFlux + R2DBC (implemented; source of truth)
- `/frontend` — React + TypeScript + Vite

Do **not** modify backend code unless explicitly requested.

## Frontend Stack

- React, TypeScript, Vite
- Tailwind CSS, React Router, Axios

## Architecture

Prefer:

```
src/
  api/
  components/
  hooks/
  layouts/
  pages/
  router/
  types/
  utils/
```

Use reusable components whenever possible.

## Coding Style

- Functional components only
- Prefer composition over duplication; keep components small
- Avoid unnecessary libraries
- Use async/await
- Keep TypeScript types explicit

## Backend Integration

Never invent APIs. Only use existing endpoints:

- `POST /messages`
- `GET /messages?receiverPhone=`
- `PATCH /messages/{messageId}/open`

If an API is missing, ask before implementing.

## Workflow

- Explain the implementation plan before generating code
- Implement one feature at a time
- Do not generate large amounts of unnecessary code
- Preserve the existing project structure
